# WeVolunteer — Better Stack heartbeat URLs.
#
#   sudo install -m 0640 -o root -g wev deploy/heartbeats.env.example /etc/wevolunteer/heartbeats.env
#
# Each value is a heartbeat's base URL from Better Stack → Uptime → Heartbeats,
# of the form https://uptime.betterstack.com/api/v1/heartbeat/<token>. The token
# is a credential: anyone holding it can mark the job healthy. This file only.
#
# Leaving one unset is allowed — the job still runs and logs that it is not
# monitored. Configure each heartbeat's period and grace in Better Stack:
#
#   BACKUP       expect every 1 day,   grace 2 hours   (wevolunteer-backup.timer, 03:00)
#   CF_REFRESH   expect every 7 days,  grace 1 day     (wevolunteer-cf-ip-refresh.timer)
#   HOST         expect every 15 min,  grace 15 min    (wevolunteer-host-check.timer)
#
# HOST reports `fail` with a list of problems (disk, memory, restart loop,
# /ready, nginx, origin certificate, backup age), so point its alerting at a
# human. See docs/operations/observability.md § Host heartbeats.

# HEARTBEAT_URL_BACKUP=https://uptime.betterstack.com/api/v1/heartbeat/REPLACE_ME
# HEARTBEAT_URL_CF_REFRESH=https://uptime.betterstack.com/api/v1/heartbeat/REPLACE_ME
# HEARTBEAT_URL_HOST=https://uptime.betterstack.com/api/v1/heartbeat/REPLACE_ME
